  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Thursday)\nIssued at 1259 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nShowers and storms may be ongoing into the day Friday before\ndissipating or spreading east of the local forecast area.\nOtherwise, dry and somewhat cooler weather is expected Friday with\nthe return of unseasonably hot weather beginning Saturday. Various\nguidance members suggest MCS development across KS either Saturday\nor early Sunday and these complex spreading southeast toward the\nregion with a weakening trend into the building upper ridge.\nConfidence is low in this scenario as the spread in timing and\nlocation remains high, however the overall pattern does support\nthis potential so expect notable adjustments in forecast rain\nchances once a scenario gains agreement. Temps on Saturday will be\nlargely dependent on the coverage and duration of any showers and\nstorms, but the trend will remain for hotter weather building\nthrough the weekend into the middle of next week. Heat advisories\nappear likely at some point during this period. The next potential\ncold front and increasing rain chances arrives toward the middle\nto latter part of next week.",
